lisa-design:
- Hardened security contexts are template-level defaults (ccf-app.apiPodSecurityContext / ccf-app.apiSecurityContext) used only when api.* AND the global podSecurityContext/securityContext are empty. Rejected putting them in values.yaml: that would silently stop the existing global security contexts from reaching the API pod (a break for installs that set them). The defaults are listed in values.yaml comments.
- runAsNonRoot/runAsUser are container-level, not pod-level: generate-public-key (alpine, `apk add openssl`) must run as root with a writable root FS. Pod level carries only fsGroup 65532 + seccomp RuntimeDefault; the publickey emptyDir is group 65532 and the openssl output is 0644, so the API can read it.
- /tmp emptyDir is mounted in the API container, migrate-db and create-user; api v0.21.0 writes only to os.TempDir() (jwt_bootstrap lock, multipart >32 MiB). Main server never calls BootstrapJWTKeyPair, so no key files are written with chart-provided keys.
